Package: q-sunshine-pve
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: q-sunshine contributors <q-sunshine@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/LizardByte/Sunshine
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Description: native PVE Console terminal broker for headless QEMU Display1
 This package contains the q-sunshine Sunshine build for QEMU Display1 D-Bus
 capture, one node-level terminal service, its VM-scoped QSF companion, and
 the Proxmox VE 9 Console-menu integration. PVE's stock VM.Console-protected
 API session is the authorization boundary; the protected PVE route passes a
 typed local descriptor request to the terminal service and never exports a
 VNC ticket, PVE cookie, CSRF token, or separate Sunshine/Moonlight PIN.
 .
 It intentionally contains no X11, Wayland, PulseAudio, or ALSA host runtime
 dependency. It is designed for Proxmox VE 9 on Debian 13 (Trixie), with
 root-managed private per-VM Display1 D-Bus and virtio-serial QSF sockets.
